Relative newbie (made it to the castle just once so far) checking in
here to offer a contrary opinion:

I am not at all disturbed by the possibility of pudding farming. I
don't think that its presence diminishes the interest of the game.
Maybe it's somewhat abusive. Maybe it should be removed/toned down.
But it didn't scare me away from playing Nethack. (Others may have had
a different reaction.) Pudding farming from the moment I heard of it
was just a way of getting lots and lots of stuff. I was never under
the impression that it was required to ascend, or the best way to
ascend, or the fastest way to ascend, or....

Since I'm a pack rat (in-game and in RL), getting lots and lots of
stuff is fine with me. I haven't personally set up a pudding farm yet:
it sounds kinda boring (the version that runs on my OS doesn't accept
copy/pasted input, so macros aren't a possibility). On the whole, I
kinda like that there is a mechanism in place that will allow you to
get nearly anything you want / almost everything there is to get, with
sufficient time and patience, since there are so many things in
nethack that are necessary (or highly desirable, or really useful, or
just fun to have) that are not guaranteed by other strategies.

And as for the "reasons for explore mode" conversation: I played in
explore mode almost exclusively for the first year or so after
discovering Nethack. As far as I'm concerned, explore mode = "easy-
game-for-kiddies-and-newbies" mode: I learned about a whole bunch of
stuff that I would have hated to find out in a permadeath context
(before I started reading all the spoilers), although it also left a
few bad habits (such as "just keep bashing it and it'll die
eventually": that tends to kill me a lot...).

My two cents.

